{
  "category": "Ball Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a POKé BALL, they have zapped many people.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a POKé BALL, they have zapped many people.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said to camouflage itself as a POKé BALL. It will self-destruct with very little stimulus.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It was discovered when POKé BALLS were introduced. It is said that there is some connection.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the study of this POKéMON, it was discovered that its components are not found in nature.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "VOLTORB was first sighted at a company that manufactures POKé BALLS. The link between that sighting and the fact that this POKéMON looks very similar to a POKé BALL remains a mystery.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "VOLTORB is extremely sensitive - it explodes at the slightest of shocks. It is rumored that it was first created when a POKé BALL was exposed to a powerful pulse of energy.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It bears an uncanny and unexplained resemblance to a POKé BALL. Because it explodes at the slightest shock, even veteran TRAINERS treat it with caution.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "A life-form whose identity is unknown. It is said to SCREECH or suddenly SELFDESTRUCT.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a POKé BALL, it has zapped many people.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It looks just like a Poké Ball. It is dangerous because it may electrocute or explode on touch.",
